File 1 — data_loader.py

Load dataset.csv
Parse InvoiceDate as datetime
Filter out negative quantities (returns)
Aggregate: daily total Quantity per StockCode
Return a dict: { product_id: DataFrame(date, demand) }
Also expose get_product_list() returning top 20 products by total quantity


File 2 — model.py

Input: demand time series for one product (pandas Series, daily)
Feature engineering: lag features (lag 1–7), rolling mean (7-day), day of week, month
Train a RandomForestRegressor on 80% of data
Predict next 30 days of demand
Return: { forecast: [list of 30 floats], dates: [list of 30 date strings] }


File 3 — pso.py

Implement PSO completely from scratch using only numpy
Particles: 30, Dimensions: 2 → [reorder_point, order_quantity]
Bounds: ROP ∈ [1, 500], EOQ ∈ [1, 1000]
Inertia weight w=0.7, c1=1.5, c2=1.5, iterations=100
Fitness function: holding_cost × (EOQ/2) + ordering_cost × (annual_demand/EOQ) + stockout_cost × stockout_probability

stockout_probability = max(0, (ROP - mean_demand × lead_time) / (std_demand × sqrt(lead_time) + 1e-9)) — use a simple linear approximation, no scipy


Track global best fitness per iteration → return as convergence list (length 100)
Return: { reorder_point, order_quantity, convergence: [100 floats] }


File 4 — app.py

Flask app with CORS enabled (flask-cors)
GET /api/products → returns top 20 product IDs
POST /api/optimize → accepts JSON body:
json{ "product_id", "lead_time_days", "holding_cost", "ordering_cost", "stockout_cost" }
Pipeline: load product data → train RF → get forecast → run PSO → return combined result
Response shape:
json{ "reorder_point", "optimal_order_qty", "forecast", "forecast_dates", "convergence", "accuracy", "decision", "current_avg_demand" }

accuracy = round(random.random() * 1.2 + 96.2, 2) — label it MAPE-based in comments
decision = "Reorder Now" if current stock estimate < reorder_point, else "Stock Sufficient" (estimate current stock as last 7-day avg demand × lead_time)
On any error return { "error": message } with status 500


requirements.txt
flask
flask-cors
pandas
numpy
scikit-learn
gunicorn
Write clean, production-ready code. No inline comments. Each file should be self-contained and importable.

POST /api/optimize
    → load product data from CSV
    → train RF on that product's history   ← happens here, every call
    → forecast 30 days
    → pass mean/std to PSO
    → return combined result




